 no  strikes and the pitch is swinging a fly  ball into right field larnick with the  play  will pollen catch near the track and  that's the inning st louis doesn't score  gets a hit leaves one after one with two  outs  runner in scoring position and it's  going to be up to andrew tim simmons 1-0  to simmons and a ball line to left and a  base hit  sono being waved around third and he  will score  and the twins get a two-out hit from  andrewton simmons to take the first lead  nice hitting there by andrea simmons and  this is what you don't see when you hit  eighth in the national league  you don't see a little spin and breaking  ball or half a cutter kind of thing  right in the middle of the plate but  simmons takes advantage of it gets an  rbi and puts his team ahead  captain jackson a spot start for a  former twin jose barrios  and a breaking ball we'll wrap that at  that up for jacks his second strikeout  went away here is dylan carlson it'll  line her to right his first time up  sono right behind the bag to the bag  two down aronado will back and the 1-2  pitch has popped up  behind the plate garver he's got room  flips the mask away on the grass he's  got it and that's out number three  so jacks three scoreless innings st  louis leaves one  cardinals that may be in business here  with bader at the plate infield in with  the ball in the outfield  and he does vader with a high fly ball  in two left brooker with the catch  o'neal tagging up  and the game is tied harrison boehner  ties it up  sac fly into left and he drives in his  26th  here's the pitch that's lying to the  shark stop to young  off the bat of miguel cino even the best  players are going to give a little bit  and i wish we had a better angle you  could kind of see  exactly where it was coming from the  other side but you can't  fault goldie in that situation because  that is a broken wrist  waiting to happen that's why leblanc has  been careful with ceno here's nick  gordon  popped up on the infield leblanc  will make the catch athlete right there  look at that play  all over that chevy call to the pen and  the cardinals turn it over to ryan  hellsley he has been tremendous  with inherited runners and now it's max  kepler  outside corner and struck him out good  work by  helsley the base hit simmons and then  the strikeout  paul goldschmidt leading off the sixth  inning tyler duffy is the new pitcher  get up the middle base head into center  well for the criticals  that is just their third hit and it's  hit number 1500  in the career paul goldschmidt 1500 hits  now the crowd  acknowledges hit number 1500 for paul  goldsmith  here in the bottom of the sixth tommy  edmond does have a grand slam in his  career  364 with the bases loaded in the 1-2  pitch  edmond it is fair inside the right field  line  two runs will score here comes another  throw to the plate not in time  tommy edmond clears the bases  cardinals on top 4-1 so really good at  that by tommy edmond  a little jumpy on the first breaking  ball didn't see the first fastball so  what does he do like he always does he  slows himself down  he gets a bad bad pitch as a breaking  ball to him i think  especially in the strike zone and just  does what you're supposed to do with it  just hit a line  drive you don't try to do too much in  that situation and what a huge at-bat  and especially  hitting a double right there with  harrison bader on first base you know  he's coming around to score nolan  arenado cardinals two for six with  runners in scoring position  and the one base hit into right  here comes goldie the wave of men the  throw to the plate  as they miss the cut they'll throw  behind nolan aronado he's in a rundown  and they avoid the tag but he's out of  the baseline  the run will score a nice insurance run  good base running  by goldschmidt and arenado comes through  and coming on the pitch in the ninth  inning the cardinal closer and all-star  alex reyes i think it's interesting that  alex reye